course: dictionary
lesson: 1676
title: Reading clues: choppy
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: On the sea or a lake, «choppy» means full of small, rough waves that the wind makes. «Big waves are scary, but boats are built to handle choppy water; seasickness makes fear feel worse.» The word water tells you that choppy is about the sea.
explain: About writing, «choppy» means broken into short, jerky parts that do not flow well. A teacher might say, «Your sentences are choppy — try joining some with "and" or "because".» The word sentences is the clue here.
explain: Hair can be choppy too, cut in uneven layers on purpose. Each time you meet the word, ask: is it about water, writing or hair? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Choppy» means full of small, rough waves when it describes the sea or a lake.
fact: «Choppy» can also describe writing that is broken into short, jerky parts that do not flow well.
fact: «Choppy» can describe hair that is cut in uneven layers on purpose.
fact: Choppy water can make boat trips bumpy and can make people seasick, so swimmers and kayakers must take care.
exercise: «Big waves are scary, but boats are built to handle choppy water.» What does choppy mean here? | Calm and flat, like glass | Very quiet and still | *Full of small, rough waves made by the wind | Sweet and warm
exercise: Your teacher writes, «Your sentences are choppy.» What does choppy mean here? | *Broken into short, jerky parts that do not flow well | Cut in long, neat layers | Full of rough waves | Covered in soft, smooth paint
exercise: Which word describes hair cut in uneven layers on purpose? | Shiny | *Choppy | Tangled | Tidy
test: The lake was choppy after the wind got up. What does choppy mean? | *Full of small, rough waves | Sweet to taste | Hot and dry | Still and smooth
test: «The story was choppy; it stopped and started every line.» What does choppy mean here? | Full of rough waves | Cut in uneven layers on purpose | *Broken into short, jerky parts | Long and flowing
exam: In «The boat rocked on the choppy sea», which word is the clue that tells you choppy is about the water? | Choppy | *Sea | Boat | Rocked
